<section class="terms">
  <h2>Terms and Conditions and Data Privacy Notice</h2>
  <p>Before creating your account, please read and understand how your information and documents will be managed within CN FILEHUB.</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Purpose of Data Collection.</strong> Your personal and academic information is collected for student identification, account management, document submission, submission tracking, and management of graduate research and thesis records.</li>
    <li><strong>Document Storage.</strong> CN FILEHUB may store thesis manuscripts, research papers, revisions, supporting documents, and other authorized graduate academic records submitted through the system.</li>
    <li><strong>Access to Documents.</strong> Students may only access their own submitted documents and submission records. Authorized College of Nursing and Graduate Program personnel may access records when necessary for review, administration, document management, and archival purposes.</li>
    <li><strong>Use of Submitted Documents.</strong> Submitted documents will be used only for legitimate academic, administrative, review, tracking, and archival purposes related to the Graduate Program.</li>
    <li><strong>Data Confidentiality.</strong> Student information and submitted files are managed through controlled access based on the user's role and authorized responsibilities within the system.</li>
    <li><strong>Data Retention.</strong> Student records and submitted documents may be retained as institutional academic and archival records according to applicable institutional policies and requirements.</li>
    <li><strong>Graduate Research Repository Consent.</strong> Your thesis or research paper will not automatically be published or included in the Graduate Research Repository. Separate consent will be requested during document submission. Repository inclusion will only proceed when the student provides consent and the document is approved by authorized personnel.</li>
    <li><strong>Appropriate System Use.</strong> CN FILEHUB must only be used for legitimate academic and administrative purposes. Users must not attempt to access, modify, download, or view records belonging to other students without authorization.</li>
    <li><strong>Account Security.</strong> You are responsible for keeping your account and password secure. Sharing your account credentials with another person is prohibited.</li>
    <li><strong>Accuracy of Information and Documents.</strong> You are responsible for ensuring that the personal information and documents submitted through the system are accurate, complete, and appropriate for academic submission.</li>
  </ol>
</section>
